llowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/userhaj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T18:46:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T18:46:08Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/50 mentions _get_drag_data() and works really well with ItemList. \r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends ItemList\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tadd_item(\"/path/to/folder\") \r\n\r\nfunc _get_drag_data(at_position: Vector2) -> Variant:\r\n\tvar folder: String = get_item_text(get_item_at_position(at_position)) #use meta data in actual code\r\n\tget_window().drag_files(PackedStringArray([folder]))\r\n```\r\n\r\nMinimal example allows dragging of folders using above method. The GDScript does not change files, but if you drag from the example onto your OS, the OS will copy the folders! Be careful!\r\n[minimal_drag_drop_files.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29714309/minimal_drag_drop_files.zip)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4896474125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]